Why separate the Product Catalog from Policies?

In enterprise insurance platforms (such as Guidewire, Duck Creek, and Sapiens), products are templates, while policies are customer-specific contracts. A single product (e.g., Comprehensive Motor Gold Plan 2026) can be used to issue thousands of individual policies. Separating these concerns enables insurers to version products, adjust pricing and rules for future sales, and maintain historical policies without retroactively changing the contracts already issued.

