Why separate Quotes, Proposals, and Applications?

Enterprise insurance platforms intentionally divide these into distinct business entities because they represent different stages of the customer journey:

Quote – An estimated premium generated from customer inputs, with no legal commitment.
Proposal – The customer's formal intent to purchase, including selected coverage and supporting information.
Application – The complete submission sent into the underwriting workflow, where it is evaluated and ultimately approved, rejected, or converted into an issued policy.

Keeping these stages separate provides full auditability, supports multiple quote revisions, enables marketplace comparisons, and preserves historical records even if no policy is ultimately issued.
